## New here? — orientation for readers unfamiliar with this tree

- **The contract is [`campaign.md`](campaign.md)**: mission, the frozen metric, levers, caps,
  verification checks, promotion rules. It is the one document a human reviews and signs off. Its
  §Decision record tail is the campaign's append-only "why" ledger.
- **Rules bind automatically.** Byte-identical [`CLAUDE.md`](CLAUDE.md) and [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md)
  give Claude Code and Codex the same §Where things live map; their matching project twins live two
  levels above. What is FROZEN stays frozen: do not edit this campaign to satisfy a
  newer kit or validator (see the kit's `docs/MIGRATING.md` instead).
- **Results live in `results/`**: `scoreboard.tsv` is the numeric record (one row per experiment),
  `JOURNAL.md` the campaign's working memory (NEXT pointer, where we stand, what to try next),
  `logbook.md` the full narrative record — the runner writes both records; the agent's record goes
  through `run_campaign.py --record`. The
  physkit version this campaign was scaffolded under is stamped at the top of the logbook and in
  `campaign.md`'s header — that pin recovers the exact kit it runs with.
- **Ad-hoc exploration does not belong here.** Work with no frozen metric goes in a project session
  (`../../sessions/<date>_<slug>/`); everything in this tree is driven by the metric above.

## How the loop runs — the two roles

The driver (`scripts/run_campaign.py --supervise`) alternates two spawned agents, each receiving only
what its job needs. It also holds `results/.supervisor.lock`, so a second Claude/Codex supervisor refuses
before campaign-body mutation or spend; the persistent file is diagnostics, not proof that an owner is still live.
Before switching harnesses, stop the supervisor and run
`python scripts/sync_agent_instructions.py --check`. Drift halts preflight and every model spawn; repair
requires an explicit `--scope campaign --from claude --write` (or `--from agents`) choice; repeat with
`--scope project` when the project pair is authoritative.
The default verifier policy preserves Claude's nested-refuter flow and gives Codex one fresh direct-refuter
thread at the worker's model per ready block; Codex debt is validated before the planner or another worker runs.

Codex loads this campaign's `.codex/hooks.json` only after the project-local hook is trusted. Start a
fresh Codex task from this campaign root, run `/hooks`, and review/trust the exact definition before a
run or resume. The hook synchronously routes canonical `apply_patch` writes to the same promotion policy
Claude uses. Keep any protected promotion in its own single-file patch so its evidence cannot be changed
atomically beside it. The scaffold validator checks the file and command, but cannot establish host trust.

The roles are:

- **The worker** executes ONE experiment per spawn, following the numbered loop in
  [`roles/worker.md`](roles/worker.md): a-priori prediction *first* (the runner refuses to spend an
  evaluation without one), run, evaluate against the frozen metric, complete the ledgers, verify
  before any promotion. Its iteration contract makes every unit cold-resumable — the ledger is the
  loop's only memory.
- **The planner** runs strategy every N units ([`roles/planner.md`](roles/planner.md)): rewrites the
  `results/queue.json` ordering, revives shelved directions a promotion has re-opened, prunes dead
  ones with a recorded rationale. It never runs experiments.

Every spawned prompt carries the role's brief by value — `campaign.md` (minus its append-only
record), the role file, the project's §Standing constraints (`../../PROJECT.md`), the JOURNAL (whole),
the worker's unit and the ledger's last rows — so a fresh agent orients from the prompt, never by
reading the tree; the driver prints the brief's size at preflight and at every spawn. A human attending the loop acts as
its **concierge** (the `run-campaign` skill): launch, watch, steer through notes in `results/inbox/`
— never by-hand execution. The same gates apply either way.

## Who reads what, when

| File | Who reads it | When |
|---|---|---|
| `campaign.md` | both roles + the human | every cycle (compiled into the spawn prompt); at sign-off |
| `CLAUDE.md` · `AGENTS.md` | Claude Code · Codex, respectively | auto-loaded, every turn; must agree |
| `roles/worker.md` · `roles/planner.md` | that role only | every spawn (compiled into the prompt) |
| `../../PROJECT.md` | everyone; §Standing constraints is injected into every spawn | background depth, on demand |
| `results/JOURNAL.md` | both roles | every cycle (the working memory — NEXT, where we stand, hypotheses, what to try next, traps, open questions — is compiled whole into the prompt; the worker brings it up to date every unit) |
| `results/scoreboard.tsv` · `results/logbook.md` | the runner writes both (the permanent record); the agent's slots and cells go through `--record`, and `--show <exp>` prints one entry | appended every experiment; the ledger's last rows are compiled into the prompt |
| `predictions/<exp>.json` | the runner's spend gate; written by the worker BEFORE each solve | per experiment |
| `results/queue.json` | the driver's unit ledger (driver is its sole writer); planner rewrites the order | per unit / per planner pass |
| `results/queue_drop/` | proposals + declinations, dropped by the runner (`--record --propose` / `--decline`); the driver merges them | per unit |
| `configs/loop.json` | the driver and its checks | at launch; hot-reloaded |
| `LITERATURE.md` *(when present)* | planner (idea roadmap) · worker (cite sources) | per the literature rule |
| `tests/correctness_checks.py` | the runner, every experiment | green-gates promotion |
